  <ym-title|Free horizon convergence><label|free-horizon-convergence>

  Source revision <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  Manuscript <verbatim|manuscript/existence/free-horizon-convergence.tex>.
  This unit proves the coefficient-space convergence input of the selected
  stationary-history handoff, using the already proved free strip estimates,
  positive roots, curvature lift and finite precision tower.

  <section|Correspondence><label|correspondence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Retort.Fleet>, <verbatim|.Fleet.lives>,
    <verbatim|.reads>, <verbatim|.muster>, <verbatim|.narrower>,
    <verbatim|.amalgam>, <verbatim|.rally>, <verbatim|.crest>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Mast.lean>: coordinate compactness,
    preserved exponential bound, narrower weighted convergence, symbol and
    finite period readout convergence, unique cluster limits. The manuscript
    gives elementary diagonal extraction and finite-head/tail proofs; it also
    proves period recovery rather than invoking an unnamed injection.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.OnTrack.far_mass>, <verbatim|.ltd>,
    <verbatim|.sales>, <verbatim|.soldY>, <verbatim|.dusty>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Yards.lean>: actual recursively built
    trains, decreasing nonnegative squared drive and increasing bounded noise
    list. Private USD/swatch/nozzle_tick were inspected; monotonicity
    compares the same initial scale with successive history depths, not
    arbitrary trains.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.OnTrack.plane>, <verbatim|.settled>,
    <verbatim|.above_the_wing>, <verbatim|.arrival>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Destination.lean>: seed
    divided-difference limit, eventual centered representatives, high-alias
    extension to Cover with summable product inverse-square majorant;
    positive limiting directional covariance uses the noise contribution
    \<gtr\>=1/k. Its high-alias divisor is <verbatim|divisor mass
    (p+reciprocal z)>, not divisor at unit physical momentum.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.OnTrack.blade>, <verbatim|.presentT>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Tugs.lean>: pulse/dual rows and fixed
    adjacent transport symbols. Private coins and lorries were read.
    Positivity of limits is verified before inverting directional, rho and
    tabE scalars. Fixed adjacent L means the final Fourier reconstruction is
    a finite alias sum; this differs from the increasing mass-side high-alias
    sum.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Retort.Parade> and <verbatim|.prod>,
    <verbatim|.opp>, <verbatim|.demise>, <verbatim|.refs>, <verbatim|.boost>,
    <verbatim|.dash>, <verbatim|.sheds>, <verbatim|.bequest>,
    <verbatim|.cap>, <verbatim|.note>, <verbatim|.priors>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Retirement.lean>: all row operations
    retain convergence with positive strip width. Divided differences are
    treated on the dense set away from their coordinate zero and recovered by
    continuity of cluster symbols, with the independently proved width loss.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Retort.dominant>, <verbatim|.concord>,
    <verbatim|.angular>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Flour.lean>: bed
    and transport primitives, amendment inverse, and exact curvature row. The
    existing curvature-horizon-producer.tex supplies explicit rollFunds
    algebra; this unit applies the convergence operations to the same
    formula.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Retort.gilt>, <verbatim|.painted>,
    <verbatim|.evening>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Astute.lean>:
    positivity survives the finite matrix limit and identifies the unique
    positive square root from its square. No continuity assertion for
    arbitrary square-root choices.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Marvel>, <verbatim|.strongBottom>,
    <verbatim|.reapsY>, <verbatim|.Exhibits>, <verbatim|.wardrobe>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Wheels.lean>: actual free horizon is
    selected with positive root values at every torus; common stagewise
    prices and both possible adjacent stage transitions were read. Static
    existence/prices are reused from the positive-row and curvature-horizon
    units.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Bid.Committed>, <verbatim|.pinsT>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Pins.lean>: retains same beds/A0/T and
    exact Replaces plus SqActs of glow. No new tower unrelated to those
    identities is selected in the proof.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Loom>, <verbatim|.Mite>,
    <verbatim|.Amplify>, <verbatim|.stellar>, <verbatim|.relayT>, private
    <verbatim|.deliver>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Train/Miracles.lean>:
    all five bed rows and five tower rows. deliver obtains mf/mn/o via exact
    torus products and applies crest at the unbounded prescribed period
    sequence. Root positivity and squared row convergence are separate
    premises of evening; both are verified before use. Cover strips are the
    actual fixed-stage paid prices, not bounds inferred from one finite
    torus.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Mathematical reuse><label|mathematical-reuse>

  No new literature substitution: the free-kernel estimates/component
  estimates, kernel-transport identities, positive-row producer,
  curvature-horizon producer and finite precision tower supply the static
  estimates and identities. This unit adds their convergence along the actual
  history. Elementary dominated convergence, Fourier coefficient recovery and
  finite-dimensional spectral decomposition are proved or explained at their
  application.

  <section|Status and checks><label|status-and-checks>

  All listed source files inspected by bounded rg/sed/cat reads. The
  correspondence uses the pinned source only. SHA256 computed for draft;
  independent review pending. No Lean build, source edit or axiom replay; not
  yet integrated, built or rendered. This does not itself prove the
  stationary annulus estimate or nonlinear flux production.

